  "id": "under-the-cat",
  "name": "Under the Cat",
  "description": "Velvet's street at the foot of the cliffs, quieter and cleaner than outsiders expect. High on the cliff face above it sits the Cat, a giant neon cat in pink and violet tubes on a girder frame, looking out over the city, and on the cliff top above the Cat, the pale government buildings of the Shelf. Along the street: a bathhouse under a curved tiled roof, paper lanterns either side of its split curtain and steam from a vent; a narrow old hotel with a violet neon strip and a lit lobby behind its glass door; a little all-night tea counter with two stools; and the Glass Orchid's discreet front, a heavy dark door under a brass lamp with a glowing glass orchid in the round window above it. Paper lanterns are strung across the street, and an old street lamp stands at the corner.",
